      <body xml:id="praepA_transl">
         <div type="section" xml:id="praep_A_ch1_transl" n="1">
            <head>Preaparatio A - translation</head>


            <div type="fragment" n="a_3.A">
               <head>α 3.A</head>
               <p>
                  <seg>
                     <term ref="#journee"/>αὐτόκερας: (It means) αὐτοκέραστον (‘self-mixed’) and
                     συμμέτρως κεκρασμένον (‘conveniently mixed’), that is, naturally disposed for
                     mixing. It is also used adverbially.</seg>
               </p>
            </div>
            
            <div type="fragment" n="a_23.A">
               <head>α 23.A</head>
               <p>
                  <seg xml:id="praep_A_seg2">
                     <term ref="#journee"/>ἀπιστίαν βλέπει (‘[A man] who has an untrustworthy look’): Eupolis (fr. 332) [writes thus]. It means [one who is] most unreliable.</seg>
               </p>
            </div>
          

         </div>
